{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovNormalisation"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.bond_pp_nn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.bond_pp_nn","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovBondRule.lean#L202-L220","doc":"A proton-proton bond (`d = 0`) contributes exactly `z`, and a\nneutron-neutron bond (`d = -h`) contributes exactly `z̄` — the two are bar\nimages of one another, by `markovZ_sub_h`. Conditional on `BondRule`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.BondRule.tr_mul_sigmaPlus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.BondRule.tr_mul_sigmaPlus","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovBondRule.lean#L198-L198","doc":"**The bond rule.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.BondRule.Unused","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.BondRule.Unused","kind":"def","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovBondRule.lean#L196-L196","doc":"`g` is not used by `x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.BondRule.sigmaPlus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.BondRule.sigmaPlus","kind":"def","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovBondRule.lean#L194-L194","doc":"The bond letter `σ_g + d·I` at generator `g`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.BondRule.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.BondRule.mul","kind":"def","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovBondRule.lean#L192-L192","doc":"Algebra multiplication. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.BondRule.tr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.BondRule.tr","kind":"def","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovBondRule.lean#L190-L190","doc":"The Jones–Markov trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.BondRule.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.BondRule.mk","kind":"ctor","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovBondRule.lean#L188-L188","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.BondRule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.BondRule","kind":"class","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovBondRule.lean#L174-L200","doc":"**The one trace-level input, carried as a hypothesis and never discharged.**\n\n`tr` is the Jones–Markov trace, `mul` the algebra multiplication, and `sigmaPlus\ng d` the bond letter `σ_g + d·I`. The field says that appending a bond letter at\na generator the element does not use multiplies the trace by `z + d`.\n\nThis is **measured, not proved** — 16 nuclei numerically to `4.45e-31`, six\nsymbolically. The mechanism is multiplicativity of the trace across an unused\ngenerator (the two sides then lie in commuting subalgebras) followed by the\nMarkov property; formalising that chain is bean `qou-g8i1`.\n\nIt is a genuine hypothesis in the §3b-cond sense: the field is a\nparameter-quantified equation in the shape of the claim, not a marker, and no\ninstance is provided. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.bondFactor_mirror_cancel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.bondFactor_mirror_cancel","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovBondRule.lean#L156-L172","doc":"**The bond factors cancel out of the mirror-crossed ratio.**\n\nGiven the product form, a nucleus `(Z,N)` contributes `z^(Z-1)` from its\nproton-proton bonds and `z̄^(N-1)` from its neutron-neutron bonds, and its\nmirror `(N,Z)` evaluated at `1/q` contributes the *same two factors* with the\nroles exchanged. They cancel identically, for **any** exponents — which is why\nthe mirror offset does not depend on the nucleus.\n\nStated about arbitrary ring elements so that it is independent of everything\nelse in this file: `zz` and `zb` stand for the two bond factors and `w`, `wb`\nfor the interface factor and its bar image. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.mirrorP_bar_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.mirrorP_bar_sub","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovBondRule.lean#L143-L154","doc":"**The mirror offset vanishes to order exactly 5.**\n\n`q¹² P(1/q) - P(q) = (q-1)⁵ (q+1)³ (q²+1)²`. The right side is a product of\npowers of `q-1`, `q+1` and `q²+1`, with `(q-1)` appearing to the fifth power —\nso the offset is `O(h⁵)` at the classical point, and that order is derived\nrather than observed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.mirrorP_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.mirrorP_eq","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovBondRule.lean#L132-L141","doc":"**`P` is the interface's Markov weight, denominators cleared.**\n\n`P = 12 q⁵ (q²+1) (z + dIface)`. So `P` is not an independent object: the\ndegree-10 polynomial, its leading coefficient and the `12` are all read off the\nsingle interface letter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.markovZ_sub_h","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.markovZ_sub_h","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovBondRule.lean#L119-L130","doc":"**The neutron-neutron bond lands on the bar image of `z`.**\n\n`z - h = z(1/q)` exactly. Under the bar involution `q ↦ q⁻¹` the Markov\nparameter `z` and the neutron-neutron bond factor `z - h` are exchanged, which\nis precisely the statement that bar acts as proton↔neutron conjugation on the\nbond letters. Nothing about this is forced by the shapes involved; it is an\nidentity special to convention D. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.markovZ_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.markovZ_inv","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovBondRule.lean#L103-L117","doc":"The bar image of the Markov parameter in closed form:\n`z(1/q) = 1 / (q (q² + 1))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.mirrorP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.mirrorP","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovBondRule.lean#L98-L101","doc":"The degree-10 polynomial governing the mirror law. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.dIface","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.dIface","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovBondRule.lean#L94-L96","doc":"The coefficient of the single proton-neutron interface letter,\n`d = -h(1/2 - f/4)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.flavorSplit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.flavorSplit","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovBondRule.lean#L90-L92","doc":"The leading flavour split `f = (q-1)²(1 - q⁻⁴)/3` — `Δm/M_N`, the\nproton-neutron mass split (`prop:flavor-split-substrate`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.hq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.hq","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovBondRule.lean#L86-L88","doc":"`h = q - q⁻¹`, the coefficient carried by a neutron-neutron bond letter\n(`σ_g - h·I`, whose eigenvalues are those of `σ_g⁻¹`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.markovZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.markovZ","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovBondRule.lean#L83-L84","doc":"The convention-D Markov parameter `z = q³/(q²+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}